      "summary": "The BYU Communication Disorders Department's strategic plan was collaboratively developed in 2021, reflecting a commitment to belonging, achievement, and growth through Christlike service. The plan focuses on four main themes: Belonging, Becoming, Collaboration, and Kindness, aiming to foster equitable access, enhance student and faculty development, and reinforce a culture of respect and service. Key initiatives include redesigning the admissions process, increasing clinical outreach to underserved communities, growing the graduate program, and enhancing interprofessional educational opportunities.",
